---
import ProjectsIcon from '../assets/icons/solid/projects.svg';
---

<section
  id="projects"
  class="card bg-base-100 border border-base-300 shadow-sm"
>
  <div class="card-body">
    <h2 class="card-title text-2xl font-semibold flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
      <ProjectsIcon
        class="h-7 w-7 shrink-0 fill-primary"
        aria-label="Projects icon"
      />
      Projects
    </h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-4">
      <!-- Cohesity & Veritas Technologies -->
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content">
            Cohesity & Veritas Technologies
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 italic">
            December 2024 - Present | August 2020 - December 2024
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">System Health Insights</h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Analytics Dashboard with Frontend Leadership
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Enterprise appliance customers needed a clearer view of health
              across distributed systems. I led the dashboard's frontend
              architecture, shaping a modular Angular application for real-time
              monitoring and proactive issue detection.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>
                Established modular component patterns and frontend coding
                standards for the team
              </li>
              <li>
                Implemented interactive visualizations for live system metrics
              </li>
              <li>
                Designed the interface to remain usable across device types and
                screen sizes
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Angular, TypeScript, RxJS, NgRx, RESTful
              APIs
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                Support Engineer Triage Application
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Full-Stack Debugging Platform
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Support engineers needed logs, metrics, and diagnostics without
              moving between disconnected sources. I designed and delivered a
              unified debugging application from UX mockups through production
              deployment.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>
                Built the frontend around rapid access to critical debugging
                data
              </li>
              <li>
                Designed backend APIs to aggregate multiple diagnostic sources
              </li>
              <li>
                Reduced triage effort through automated log parsing and issue
                classification
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Angular, Node.js, TypeScript, Express.js,
              RESTful APIs
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                Release Management Automation
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                CLI Tool for Microservices Deployment
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Coordinating releases across 25+ microservices created repetitive
              work and opportunities for human error. I built a command-line
              workflow that joined release preparation, deployment, and
              validation.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>
                Automated version bumps, changelogs, and dependency updates
              </li>
              <li>
                Integrated CI/CD pipelines with rollback and validation checks
              </li>
              <li>Reduced release cycle time by 70%</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Node.js, TypeScript, CLI frameworks, Git
              APIs
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Ecozen Solutions -->
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content">
            Ecozen Solutions
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 italic">
            September 2019 - August 2020
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">IoT Analytics Dashboard</h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Real-Time Monitoring Platform
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Farm operators needed one place to monitor device performance,
              environmental conditions, and operational metrics. I built a
              responsive Vue.js dashboard for live oversight across multiple
              farms.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>Visualized live sensor data from 100+ devices</li>
              <li>Designed interactions for non-technical farm operators</li>
              <li>Surfaced critical device conditions through live alerts</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Vue.js, JavaScript, RESTful APIs, WebSockets
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                MQTT Client & Data Pipeline
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                IoT Data Processing Solution
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Heterogeneous devices produced continuous sensor streams that
              needed consistent validation and storage. I engineered the
              ingestion path from MQTT communication through MongoDB
              persistence.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>Developed MQTT client for real-time device communication</li>
              <li>
                Parsed, validated, and stored sensor data through an ETL
                pipeline
              </li>
              <li>
                Added scheduled processing and email alerts for device anomalies
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Node.js, TypeScript, MQTT, MongoDB, Express.js
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Advinans -->
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content">Advinans</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 italic">
            September 2018 - August 2019
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                Kubernetes Deployment Automation
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Slack-Integrated DevOps Bot
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              Manual container releases took 30 minutes and interrupted the
              development workflow. I created a Slack bot that authenticated,
              validated, and orchestrated deployments to Kubernetes.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>
                Reduced deployment time from 30 minutes to under 2 minutes
              </li>
              <li>
                Ran deployment logic in TypeScript on Google Cloud Functions
              </li>
              <li>
                Integrated Google Kubernetes Engine for zero-downtime releases
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> TypeScript, Google Cloud Functions, Kubernetes,
              Docker, GCP, Slack API
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- TallBird Employment Innovations -->
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-3">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-base-content">
            TallBird Employment Innovations
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70 italic">
            January 2018 - August 2018
          </p>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                Progressive Web Application
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Modern HR Platform
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              The HR product needed a reliable app-like experience across
              devices and network conditions. I designed and built a React
              progressive web application around offline use and timely updates.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>
                Achieved 90+ Lighthouse score across performance, accessibility,
                and best practices
              </li>
              <li>
                Used service workers and caching strategies for offline support
              </li>
              <li>
                Added push notifications and a responsive, mobile-first
                interface
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> React, Service Workers, Web App Manifest,
              JavaScript
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div
          class="relative rounded-2xl border border-base-300 bg-base-200 px-5 py-4"
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-2">
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-y-1">
              <h4 class="text-base font-semibold">
                Serverless Backend Architecture
              </h4>
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-base-content/80">
                Firebase-Powered Infrastructure
              </p>
            </div>
            <p class="text-sm text-base-content/80 leading-relaxed">
              To support real-time product behavior without traditional server
              operations, I designed the backend around managed Firebase
              services and automatic scaling.
            </p>
            <ul class="ml-4 list-disc text-sm text-base-content/70 space-y-1">
              <li>Implemented business logic with Firebase Cloud Functions</li>
              <li>
                Synchronized application data in real time with Cloud Firestore
              </li>
              <li>
                Designed authentication, authorization, and RESTful endpoints
                for web and mobile clients
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-2">
              <strong>Tech Stack:</strong> Firebase, Cloud Functions, Cloud Firestore,
              Node.js, JavaScript
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
